meta {
  name: 78 Messaging Reports
  seq: 78
}

docs {
  # Messaging Reports

  Business Admin › REPORT › **WhatsApp Report** / **SMS Report**. Every WhatsApp and
  SMS the tenant sent, with the provider's delivery status, read live from the
  external **Exchange** messaging gateway. This is the same data source as the legacy
  `business.kalnostic.com/subscription/business/whatsAppReport` / `smsReport` screens.

  In the app:
  - `/business-admin/report/whatsapp-report`
  - `/business-admin/report/sms-report`

  How it works:
  - The tenant is mapped to its integer `exchangeTenantId`, and every call is scoped
    to that id. A tenant without one gets 409 `EXCHANGE_TENANT_ID_MISSING`.
  - The backend calls `GET {EXCHANGE_API_URL}/notifications/items` and
    `/notifications/itemDetail` with the legacy JSON-body-on-GET envelope.
  - Nothing is stored locally. Local `communication_logs` rows, matched on
    `exchange_id`, only fill in a missing recipient or template name.
  - The page size is fixed by the gateway: `meta.limit` is usually 50. There is no
    `limit` param, no search and no sort, as on the legacy screens.
  - Dates are whole days in Indian local time, inclusive.

  Permissions (module `business_admin`, section "Reports"):
  - `business_admin:reports__view_whatsapp_report`
  - `business_admin:reports__view_sms_report`

  Business Admin holds both and bypasses the check anyway.

  Errors:
  - 400 validation or `MESSAGING_REPORT_INVALID_DATE_RANGE`
  - 403 missing permission
  - 404 `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`
  - 409 `EXCHANGE_TENANT_ID_MISSING`
  - 409 `MESSAGING_TENANT_NOT_REGISTERED`: the gateway answered "client not found!", meaning
    the business was never registered with the Exchange (SiteAdmin → register-exchange)
  - 502 `MESSAGING_GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE`
  - 503 `MESSAGING_GATEWAY_NOT_CONFIGURED`: no `EXCHANGE_API_*` env, the normal
    state on a local dev box
}
